d 'LTSCOINT': module to perform Least Trimmed Squares estimation of a cointegrated ADL with outliers
d
d    ltscoint implements the Least Trimmed Squares (LTS) estimator
d for the autoregressive distributed lag model in
d equilibrium-correction form analysed by Berenguer-Rico and
d Nielsen (2026), "Least Trimmed Squares: Cointegration and
d Outliers", Oxford Bulletin of Economics and Statistics 88,
d 690-711 (doi:10.1111/obes.70077). The h-subsample with the
d smallest residual sum of squares is found by the FAST-LTS
d concentration-step algorithm of Rousseeuw and Van Driessen (2006)
d or by exact enumeration; the remaining T-h observations are the
d outliers. Using the authors' oracle result, inference is OLS on
d the retained observations. The command reports full-sample OLS
d and LTS side by side: the coefficient table, PcGive-style
d mis-specification tests, the long-run cointegrating coefficients
d with delta-method standard errors, the
d Harbo-Johansen-Nielsen-Rahbek LR test (Gamma-approximation
d p-values from Doornik 1998, 2003) and the Ericsson-MacKinnon
d (2002) ECM t-test of no cointegration, weak-exogeneity
d regressions, and the identified outliers. A subcommand profiles
d the cumulant normality statistic over h to determine the number
d of outliers, and graph subcommands draw the paper's
d mis-specification and data figures. 
d
d KW: cointegration
d KW: least trimmed squares
d KW: autoregressive distributed lag model
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260917
d
d Author:   Merwan Roudane, NA
d Support: email  merwanroudane920@@gmail.com
d
f ltscoint.ado
f ltscoint.sthlp
f ltscoint_methods.sthlp
f ltscoint_example.do
f ltscoint_ukcons.dta
